{"type": "sena", "_data": [{"contents": [{"type": "lesson_name", "content": "Man vs. Machine"}, {"type": "unit_name", "content": "Cold Metal"}, {"type": "position", "content": 9}, {"type": "origin", "content": "stub"}, {"type": "lesson", "content": 5}, {"type": "level", "content": "B1.2"}], "type": "metadata"}, {"contents": [{"type": "test", "content": "false"}], "type": "achievment_test"}, {"contents": [{"type": "primary", "content": "Explain about technology and technical problems in communicative situations."}, {"type": "secondary_1", "content": "Identifies important and specific information and aspects of attitude and intention in conversations, texts or presentations about common technology."}, {"type": "secondary_2", "content": "Identifies important and specific information and aspects of attitude and intention in conversations, texts or presentations about common technology."}, {"type": "secondary_3", "content": "Identifies important and specific information and aspects of attitude and intention in conversations, texts or presentations about common technology."}, {"type": "secondary_4", "content": "Identifies important and specific information and aspects of attitude and intention in conversations, texts or presentations about common technology."}, {"type": "secondary_5", "content": "Identifies important and specific information and aspects of attitude and intention in conversations, texts or presentations about common technology."}, {"type": "secondary_6", "content": "Identifies important and specific information and aspects of attitude and intention in conversations, texts or presentations about common technology."}, {"type": "secondary_7", "content": "Identifies important and specific information and aspects of attitude and intention in conversations, texts or presentations about common technology."}, {"type": "secondary_8", "content": "Identifies important and specific information and aspects of attitude and intention in conversations, texts or presentations about common technology."}], "type": "objectives"}, {"contents": [{"type": "heading", "content": "Modal Verbs for Speculation"}, {"type": "describer", "content": "<p>You can use modals to talk about degrees of certainty.</p>You use them to describe what is definite, probable, possible, or impossible from the speaker's point of view."}, {"type": "text", "content": "You can use <span class=\"italic\">must</span>, <span class=\"italic\">may</span>, <span class=\"italic\">might</span>, and <span class=\"italic\">could</span> to describe degrees of certainty."}, {"type": "text", "content": "Must = You are quite sure / It's a good guess<br/>Couldn't / Can't = You are quite sure it's not / It's a good guess it's not<br/>May / Might / Can / Could = maybe<br/>May not / Might not = maybe it's not"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Creating cyborg humans may demand we use metal in our bodies."}, {"type": "example", "content": "You may think that cyborgs are those half human, half machine beings from Star Trek."}, {"type": "example", "content": "Bionic limbs must be a better alternative than those which are not."}, {"type": "example", "content": "A new electronic headset that you wear could allow you to play virtual games just by thinking."}, {"type": "example", "content": "In the future all of these things may be connected to our nervous systems."}], "type": "learning_points"}, {"contents": [{"type": "heading", "content": "Subject and Object Relative Clauses"}, {"type": "describer", "content": "You put a relative clause immediately after the noun it talks about."}, {"type": "text", "content": "You use a relative clause with <span class=\"italic\">which</span> for things to make the thing  you are talking about clearer."}, {"type": "text", "content": "In spoken English and written English, <span class=\"italic\">that</span> often replaces <span class=\"italic\">which</span> or <span class=\"italic\">who</span>. <span class=\"italic\">Which</span> is generally more formal than <span class=\"italic\">that</span>."}, {"type": "text", "content": "<span class=\"italic\">Where</span> and <span class=\"italic\">when</span> are also connectors that can begin relative clause when they modify a noun (rather than a verb)."}, {"type": "text", "content": "Relative clauses answer the question \u201cWhat kind / type of ... ? \u201c or \u201cWhich ... ?\u201d."}, {"type": "table", "content": "{\"rows\":5,\"columns\":3,\"cells\":[\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"strong\\\">Example</span>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"strong\\\">Clause</span>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"strong\\\">Relative connector</span>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"italic\\\">People who are totally colorblind can now have electronic implants that enable them to see color.</span>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"who are totally colorblind <br/>(Which people?)\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"who\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"italic\\\">A new electronic headset that you wear could allow you to play virtual games just by thinking.</span>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"that you wear<br/>(What type of headset?)\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"that\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"italic\\\">He hopes for a future where he can communicate with others mind to mind.</span>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"where he can communicate with others  mind to mind<br/>(What type of future?)\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"where\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"italic\\\">That was the day when he decided to change his future.</span>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"when he decided to change his future<br/>(Which day?)\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"when\\\"}\"],\"styles\":\"\"}"}], "type": "learning_points"}, {"contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "colorblind"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "unable to see color"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(adjective)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: People who are colorblind can now have implants that allow them to see color."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn7le05ob09aud01"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"type": "text", "content": "These are words you use to talk about cyborgs."}], "type": "target_word_describer"}, {"contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "to enable"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "to make something possible"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(verb)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: Implants enable people who are colorblind to see color."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn7le05ob09aud02"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "founder"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "the person who starts an organization"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(noun)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: Kevin Warwick is the founder of Project Cyborg."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn7le05ob09aud03"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "guinea pig"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "a test subject"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(noun)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: Kevin Warwick uses himself as a guinea pig to test his theories."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn7le05ob09aud04"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "extra-human"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "more than human"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(adjective)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: He hopes that implants will make him extra-hu