ll, melding man with machine or creating cyborg humans may demand this, at least for a while.</p>You may think that cyborgs are those half human, half machine beings from <span class=\"italic\">Star Trek</span>. They are and they aren't. There are already cyborgs that live among us.", "id": 1, "image": "engenn7le05ob09re2img01.jpg"}, {"time": "27300", "text": "There are many who have bionic limbs which operate with signals from their brains. People who are totally colorblind can now have electronic implants that enable them to see color. A new electronic headset that you wear could allow you to play virtual games just by thinking. In the future  all of these things may be connected to our nervous systems.", "id": 2, "image": "engenn7le05ob09re2img03.jpg"}, {"time": "48000", "text": "Kevin Warwick, who is the founder of Project Cyborg at the University of Reading, uses himself as the guinea pig in his cyborg experiments. He wants to become the world's most complete cyborg. This could allow him to be extra-human. He hopes for a future where he can communicate with others mind to mind.", "id": 3, "image": "engenn7le05ob09re2img02.jpg"}], "coverimg": "engenn7le05ob09re2img01.jpg"}}], "template_override": 1, "type": "audio", "id": 1, "_data": [], "title": ""}, {"contents": [{"type": "picture", "value": {"audiosrc": "engenn7le05ob09re6aud01", "images": [], "coverimg": "engenn7le05ob09re6img01.jpg"}}], "template_override": 1, "type": "audio", "id": 2, "_data": [], "title": ""}], "id": 0}]}